area: sanitize
case: 23-malformed-overlong
verification: explicit-divergence
oracle: python
projection: sanitize
reason: the oracle projection must read the corpus through a text decode (its sanitizer takes str), so an ill-formed byte arrives as U+FFFD before the escape pass runs; the port's sanitizer is byte-faithful and passes the original bytes through. The pass itself agrees on every case the walk does not touch: same count, same idempotence, same reversibility. The bytes reach the two sanitizers differently, not the rule.
